WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/driving/components/drivetrain-health/HealthOverview.tsx — a presentational leaf fed
  { overallHealth: 'good'|'warning'|'critical', healthScore: number, motorStatus: string } by the Drivetrain Health page.
  Data hooks: useTranslation only (the parent owns the query lifecycle). It renders a React fragment:
    (a) when overallHealth !== 'good' → <AlertBanner variant={getAlertVariant(overallHealth)} icon={<AlertTriangle/>}
        title={critical ? 'Critical Temperature Warning' : 'Elevated Temperatures Detected'}>
        {critical ? criticalMsg : warningMsg}</AlertBanner>   (getAlertVariant: warning→'warning', critical→'danger')
    (b) <GlassPanel glow={HEALTH_GLOW[overallHealth]} p-6> with
          left  : good ? <CheckCircle/> : <AlertTriangle/>  (h-10 w-10, tinted by healthTextClass)
                  <h2> good ? 'Drivetrain Healthy' : warning ? 'Drivetrain Running Warm' : 'Drivetrain Overheating'
                  <p>  '{t("drivetrain.motorState","Motor State")}: {motorStatus}'
          right : <Badge variant={healthBadgeVariant(overallHealth)} size="lg" dot>
                    {t(`drivetrain.health.${overallHealth}`, overallHealth.toUpperCase())}   ('GOOD'/'WARNING'/'CRITICAL')
                  <span text-2xl font-bold {healthTextClass}><AnimatedNumber value={healthScore} suffix="%"/></span>
  healthTextClass / HEALTH_COLOR : good #10b981 (emerald) · warning #f59e0b (amber) · critical #ef4444 (red).
  healthBadgeVariant : good→success · warning→warning · critical→danger.   HEALTH_GLOW : good→green · warning→cyan · critical→purple.
  AnimatedNumber renders fmtNumber(value, 0) + suffix (its default decimals is 0).

