  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO HealthOverview errors; all blockers pre-exist this change):
    Shared.xcframework staged successfully, so the gate proceeded to the app compile, where it fails on architecture-wide,
    pre-existing, committed surfaces (NOT touched by this change):
      • Duplicate top-level type declarations across TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/* surfaces — e.g. ChargeUnitPrefs,
        ChargeStateDTO, ChargeSessionDTO, ChargeLoadStatus, ChargeConnection, ChargeStatusProjection, SafetyModel,
        SafetyUpdate, SafetyLoadStatus, SafetyConnection, FleetStatsBarModel each defined in 2+ widget files →
        "ambiguous for type lookup" + cascading "cannot infer contextual base in reference to member 'loaded'/'live'/…"
        (the same parallel-merge collision class — `DashboardWidgetSize` redefined 15× — recorded by ToolCard /
        AlertMessageEditor / FSMTimelineChart in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md).
      • The app target also globs the co-located *.Tests.swift files (every feature-view + widget surface ships its tests
        this way) which `import XCTest` + `@testable import TeslaSync` into the app target — a project.yml test-target
        restructuring, outside this prompt's allowed files.
      • macOS additionally needs a development signing certificate this runner does not provision.
